### 2. YuE (7B + 1B) — **Best for Voice Style Transfer**

**Hugging Face:** `m-a-p/YuE-s1-7B-anneal-en-icl` (for voice cloning mode)

| Aspect | Details |
|--------|---------|
| **License** | Apache 2.0 |
| **Max Duration** | Several minutes (full songs) |
| **VRAM Required** | Optimized to run smoothly even on GPUs with just 8GB VRAM using quantized models; 12 GB for 8-bit quantized; under 10GB with sequential offloading (very slow) |
| **Full Quality** | 24GB+ recommended; For full song generation (4+ sessions): GPUs with at least 80GB memory |

**Voice Cloning via In-Context Learning (ICL):**
- YuE supports dual-track ICL mode! You can prompt the model with a reference song, and it will generate a new song in a similar style (voice cloning, music style transfer, etc.)
- A novel In-Context Learning framework enables advanced style transfer of voice characteristics across tracks, fundamental voice cloning, and bidirectional content creation.

**How it works:**
```bash
python infer.py \
  --stage1_model m-a-p/YuE-s1-7B-anneal-en-icl \
  --use_audio_prompt \
  --audio_prompt_path user_voice.mp3 \
  --prompt_start_time 0 \
  --prompt_end_time 30
```

User provides a 30-second vocal reference, and YuE generates new songs matching that voice style.

