## Recommended Architecture for MusicHive

### Option A: ACE-Step + LoRA Training (Most Integrated)
```
User Records Voice (30-100 min singing) 
    → Train Custom LoRA (~few hours on A100)
    → User's Voice Model Stored
    → Generate Songs with User's Voice
```

**Pros:** Single model, fastest inference
**Cons:** 30-100 mins of singing vocal samples are recommended for a voice. The more samples you provide, the more singing details AI can learn. — This is a lot for casual users

### Option B: YuE + Voice Reference (Easiest for Users)
```
User Uploads 30-sec Vocal Sample
    → Use YuE ICL Mode with Reference
    → Generate Songs in Similar Voice Style
```

**Pros:** Only 30 seconds of audio needed, zero training
**Cons:** Style transfer rather than true cloning, lower fidelity

### Option C: Music Gen + RVC Pipeline (Most Flexible)
```
Generate Song (DiffRhythm/ACE-Step)
    → Separate Vocals (Demucs/UVR5)
    → Convert Vocals (RVC with user's trained model)
    → Remix Stems
```

**Pros:** Best voice quality, users only need ~10 min of audio for RVC training
**Cons:** More complex pipeline, higher latency

